2	// AdamW — vendor-neutral algorithm header.
3	//
4	// Reference: Loshchilov & Hutter 2017, "Decoupled Weight Decay
5	// Regularization" (https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05101), Algorithm 2.
6	//
7	// Math (decoupled weight decay variant):
8	//   m_t = beta1 * m_{t-1} + (1 - beta1) * g
9	//   v_t = beta2 * v_{t-1} + (1 - beta2) * g^2
10	//   m_hat = m_t / (1 - beta1^t)        [bias correction]
11	//   v_hat = v_t / (1 - beta2^t)        [bias correction]
12	//   p -= lr * (m_hat / (sqrt(v_hat) + eps) + wd * p)
13	//
14	// Per-element step function called from inside a grid-stride loop in the
15	// per-backend launch kernel. Compiles under nvcc (CUDA) and hipcc (HIP).
16	// Pallas/JAX implements the same math directly in launch_adamw.py.
17	//
18	// Calling convention: bc1, bc2 are passed un-inverted —
19	//   bc1 = 1 - beta1^t,  bc2 = 1 - beta2^t
20	// — matching the binding code in csrc/bindings/bindings.cpp and the Python
21	// reference (`bc1 = 1.0 - beta1 ** step`). The step function divides by
22	// them to obtain the bias-corrected moments.
